Different algorithms for finding chunks
=======================================
Currently we use a first-fit approach, but it would
be nice to have a best-fit option.

Replace MEMALLOC_NEW_CHUNK_MULTIPLIER
=====================================
Currently, when we allocate a new chunk for a malloc call of n bytes, we
multiply by MEMALLOC_NEW_CHUNK_MULTIPLIER.
This is not very nice. It's best to have a function that calculates how many
extra bytes we have to allocate for future calls.


